.TH XEMU 1 "2026-08-05" "xemu 0.8.136" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xemu \- emulator for the original Xbox game console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xemu
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ \-dvd_path
.IR image.iso ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xemu
emulates the hardware of the original Microsoft Xbox (2001). It is a fork of
QEMU that models the console's NV2A graphics processor, MCPX boot ROM, APU
audio hardware, and IDE and USB peripherals, running the real Xbox kernel and
title code rather than high-level-emulating individual games.
.PP
Rendering is performed through Vulkan; audio is output via SDL2 or PipeWire.
Most configuration is done through the graphical settings dialog rather than on
the command line, and settings persist to a configuration file between runs.
.SS Required system files
.B xemu
cannot start without an Xbox MCPX boot ROM image, an Xbox BIOS image, and a
formatted hard-disk image. These are copyrighted Microsoft material and are
.B not
distributed with this package; you must supply them yourself, dumped from
hardware you own. Set their paths from the settings dialog on first launch, or
in the configuration file.
.SH OPTIONS
Because
.B xemu
descends from QEMU, it accepts many of QEMU's system-emulation options in
addition to those below. The options listed here are the ones specific to
.B xemu
or most commonly useful; see
.UR https://xemu.app/docs/
the upstream documentation
.UE
for the full set.
.TP
.BI \-dvd_path " path"
Insert the disc image at
.I path
into the emulated DVD drive at startup. Overrides the disc path stored in the
configuration file for this run only.
.TP
.BI \-config_path " path"
Read and write settings from
.I path
instead of the default per-user configuration file. Useful for keeping separate
profiles or for scripted, reproducible runs.
.TP
.B \-full\-screen
Start with the emulator window in full-screen mode.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/xemu/xemu/xemu.toml
Default per-user configuration file, holding the paths to the MCPX boot ROM,
BIOS, and hard-disk images along with input, audio, and video settings. The
exact location follows the XDG base-directory specification and can be
overridden with
.BR \-config_path .
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch the emulator and configure system images through the settings dialog:
.PP
.RS
.B xemu
.RE
.PP
Boot straight into a disc image, full screen:
.PP
.RS
.B xemu \-full\-screen \-dvd_path ~/games/title.iso
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qemu\-system\-i386 (1)
.PP
Upstream documentation:
.UR https://xemu.app/docs/
.UE
